Subject: [PATCH 08137/11362] [outer-loop] Unblock .528 activation:
 operator_override on the capstone false-positive

The conductor was in a refuse-sleep-retry loop since 09:33 EDT -- every 2 minutes it
tried to activate 2026.07.528, the exclusion-manifest linter HARD-refused on
exp5973-v528-capstone-reconciliation with SCOPE_MATCHED_PRIOR_FAILURE, activation
failed, sleep, repeat. It would not have self-cleared.

This is the false-positive class CLAUDE.md names explicitly under "Auto-override for
known-legit continuations" (2026-05-29 standing operator authorization): a capstone-vN
task scope-matches every prior milestone's capstone by construction and is structurally
never a doomed rerun. The planner was required to emit operator_override and did not.

The linter's "7 prior failures" are not failures. All five named priors are prior-
MILESTONE capstones: exp5728/5862/5903 carry `complete:` verdicts, and exp5716/5768
carry TEMPLATE PLACEHOLDER TEXT in honest_verdict -- literally "terminal summary
starting with complete: or blocked:." -- which the reconciler then classifies as
untrustworthy and counts as a failure. So the match is spurious twice over.

Applied per the documented override format. Surgical text insert, not a YAML
round-trip: 1 insertion, 0 deletions, 13 tasks before and after, parse verified.

NOT FIXED HERE, worth a separate look: the template-placeholder verdicts are a
capstone-authoring defect that will keep manufacturing phantom prior-failures for
every future capstone.

